  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains in place through the weekend with\ntemperatures continuing to warm to around or slightly above\nnormal. Saturday looks to be the warmest with afternoon highs\nrising into the mid 60s for many. Dry conditions remain in place\nthrough the weekend into the beginning of the work week.\nBeginning early next week, an upper low drops south along the\nwest coast. Increasing southerly flow looks to bring moisture\nnorth into East Idaho by Tuesday, possibly as early as late\nMonday for some. The southerly flow MAY be able to enhance\nprecipitation into portions of the central mountains late\nTuesday into Wednesday. Ensemble means dig the upper low south\ninto southern Nevada in a split flow pattern through late\nWednesday, then slowly weakens and ejects the trough northeast\nthrough the remainder of the week. Clusters tell a much\ndifferent story with significant differences in treatment of the\nsplit low. NBM appears to split the difference, keeping East\nIdaho unsettled and cool for the remainder of the week.",
